takes always, auto, or never, and
.B \-k
is accepted.
.TP
.B make
Run make rules.
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file ,
.BR \-C ", " \-\-directory ,
.B \-B
(always rebuild),
.B \-k
(keep going), and the POSIX modes
.BR \-e ,
.BR \-i ,
.BR \-S ,
.BR \-n ,
.BR \-p ,
.BR \-q ,
.BR \-r ,
.BR \-s ,
and
.B \-t
are supported, and
.B \-j
takes an optional job count passed through MAKEFLAGS. Functions include call,
eval, filter, filter-out, foreach, patsubst, shell, sort, and wildcard. The
